2026-03-03 22:26:35 [simon@midnightblue] vic20 set text color
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] On the VIC-20, you have a few options to set text color:
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] • Using POKE to color memory* (most common):
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] POKE 38400 + X, C
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] Where `X` is the screen position (0-505) and `C` is the color code (0-7):
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 0 = Black
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 1 = White
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 2 = Red
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 3 = Cyan
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 4 = Purple
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 5 = Green
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 6 = Blue
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] - 7 = Yellow
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] • Setting color for current position*:
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] POKE 646, C: PRINT "HELLO"
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] • Control characters* (CHR$ codes 1-8 for colors):
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] PRINT CHR$(5);"GREEN TEXT"
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] • At specific screen location*:
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] POKE 7680 + Y * 22 + X, ASC("A"): POKE 38400 + Y * 22 + X, 2
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] (7680/1E00 is screen memory, 38400/9600 is color memory, 22 columns wide)
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] Want a specific example or need to set border/background colors too?
2026-03-03 22:26:44 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:08:24 [simon@midnightblue] assemblers for the vic20
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] • Native VIC-20 Assemblers* (run on the hardware)
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - VICMON – The classic monitor/assembler cartridge from Commodore. POKEs, machine code,
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] basic assembly
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - PAL / VIC-PAL – Popular full-featured assembler, often used with the Super Expander
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - MAE (Macro Assembler Editor) – Powerful, later era
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - Merlin – Well-regarded, ported from Apple II
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - Famous Assembler – German, quite capable
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] • Modern Cross-Assemblers* (build on PC, output .prg)
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - ACME – Very popular, clean syntax, good VIC-20 support
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - Kick Assembler – Java-based, modern features, macros
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - TMPx – Portable, stable
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - xa (André Fachat's) – Portable, unix-friendly
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - DASM – Classic, multi-platform
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - ca65 (cc65 suite) – Powerful macro assembler, linker support
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] • IDEs*
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - CBM prg Studio – Windows IDE with built-in assembler and emulator integration
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - Relaunch64 – Java IDE for C64/VIC cross-dev
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] - VS Code – Extensions for ACME, KickAss syntax highlighting
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] Most output standard `.prg` files (load address 1001 for BASIC stub, or 1000 for auto-run ML).
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] VIC-20 memory map is tricky—use `=1001` or `=1200`+ to avoid BASIC/ZP.
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] Preference? ACME or Kick Assembler are solid modern choices.
2026-03-03 23:08:42 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:26:36 [simon@midnightblue] memory map of vic20 when 16K expansion connected
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] VIC-20 Memory Map with 16K Expansion (typically mapped at 2000-5FFF):
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $0000-$03FF  1KB  System RAM (zero page, stack, screen)
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $0400-$0FFF  3KB  Reserved/unused or 3K expansion if installed
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $1000-$1FFF  4KB  User BASIC RAM / Screen memory
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $2000-$3FFF  8KB  16K Expansion Block 1
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $4000-$5FFF  8KB  16K Expansion Block 2
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $6000-$7FFF  8KB  Free for cartridges/ROM
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $8000-$8FFF  4KB  Character ROM
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $9000-$900F       VIC-I Video registers
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $9110-$911F       VIA 1 (6522 I/O)
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $9120-$912F       VIA 2 (6522 I/O)
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $9400-$97FF  1KB  Color RAM (nibble-wide)
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $9800-$9FFF  2KB  Reserved/unused
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $A000-$BFFF  8KB  Cartridge ROM / RAM or free
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $C000-$DFFF  8KB  BASIC ROM
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] $E000-$FFFF  8KB  KERNAL ROM
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] Total RAM: 1K (base) + 4K (base) + 16K (expansion) = 21KB available to BASIC/user.
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] The 16K expansion is typically contiguous from 2000-5FFF, giving BASIC programs significantly more
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] memory (user BASIC starts at 1200 with screen at 1E00).
2026-03-03 23:26:56 [kimi-k2.5] 
