2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] I'll help you understand the bit manipulation problem. To insert a 0 between each bit of a 4-bit
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] binary number, you can use bitwise operations. Here's a simple method:
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] For a 4-bit number `abcd` (where a, b, c, d are bits), you want to transform it to `a0b0c0d`.
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] One approach is:
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 1. Spread the bits out by shifting them to higher positions
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 2. Use bitwise OR to combine them with zeros in between
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] Here's a JavaScript implementation:
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] function insertZerosBetweenBits(num) {
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// For 4-bit number: abcd -> a0b0c0d
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Spread bits: a to position 6, b to position 4, c to position 2, d to position 0
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 	return ((num & 0b1000) << 3) |  // a -> position 6
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 		   ((num & 0b0100) << 2) |  // b -> position 4
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 		   ((num & 0b0010) << 1) |  // c -> position 2
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 		   ((num & 0b0001));        // d -> position 0
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] // Example: 0b1011 (11 decimal) -> 0b10000101 (133 decimal)
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] console.log(insertZerosBetweenBits(0b1011).toString(2)); // 10000101
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] This works by:
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] - Taking each bit and shifting it left by its position index
2026-03-09 21:33:26 [deepseek-chat] - The pattern is: bit 3 (MSB) shifts 3, bit 2 shifts 2, bit 1 shifts 1, bit 0 stays
