2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] To enable interrupts on a system listening for data on a specific port, you must configure the
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] hardware abstraction layer or the specific driver handling the socket buffer.
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Below is a conceptual example of how to define an interrupt service routine (ISR) and enable global
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] interrupts in a C-based embedded environment.
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] #include <stdint.h>
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] // Define the interrupt service routine
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] void __attribute__((interrupt)) Socket_Data_ISR(void) {
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// 1. Clear interrupt flag
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// 2. Process incoming data from port 8081
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// 3. Acknowledge receipt
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] void Enable_Port_Interrupts(void) {
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// Configure NVIC or Interrupt Controller
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// Set priority and enable the specific IRQ line
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	NVIC_EnableIRQ(PORT_8081_IRQn);
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// Enable global interrupts
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	__enable_irq();
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] If you are working within a user-space application (e.g., Linux), you cannot directly "enable
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] interrupts." Instead, you must use non-blocking I/O or event-driven mechanisms like `epoll` to
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] handle incoming data efficiently.
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] #include <sys/epoll.h>
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] void Setup_Event_Loop(int socket_fd) {
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	int epoll_fd = epoll_create1(0);
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	struct epoll_event event;
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	event.events = EPOLLIN | EPOLLET; // Edge-triggered mode
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	event.data.fd = socket_fd;
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	epoll_ctl(epoll_fd, EPOLL_CTL_ADD, socket_fd, &event);
2026-03-14 17:30:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
