2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the breakdown of the two mathematical issues:
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Loop Body Cycles: A `nop [20]` instruction takes 21 cycles (1 for the instruction + 20
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] delay). Your current loop body is 42 cycles, not 39.
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	* `nop [20]` = 21
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	* `set` = 1
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	* `nop [17]` = 18
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	* `set` = 1
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	* `jmp` = 1
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	* Total = 42 cycles
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Iteration Count: Shifting `25` by 3 places (`in y, 29`) sets `y` to `200`. However, a
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] `jmp y--` loop evaluates the condition before decrementing. Entering the loop with `y =
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 200` causes it to execute 201 times (from 200 down to 0).
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 42 cycles × 201 iterations = 8442 cycles.
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] To achieve exactly 39 cycles × 200 iterations (7800 cycles), you can pre-decrement `y` once before
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] the loop and adjust the `nop` delays to sum to 39:
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	y, 25
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	in	y, 29
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	y, isr
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, stripe	; pre-decrement y to 199 for exactly 200 iterations
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] stripe:
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop	[17]		; 18 cycles
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pindirs, 1	; 1 cycle
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop	[17]		; 18 cycles
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pindirs, 0	; 1 cycle
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, stripe	; 1 cycle
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] • (Note: The 4 setup instructions before `stripe` will consume an additional 4 cycles. If those
2026-03-29 09:33:09 [gemini-3.1-pro] must be included in the strict 7800 limit, you will need to absorb them by reducing a `nop` delay
