2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] Total = 42 cycles per loop.
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 42 cycles × 200 iterations = 8,400 cycles.
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] To hit exactly 7,800 cycles, your loop body needs to be 39 cycles. You can fix this by reducing
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] your delay values to sum to 34 (e.g., `nop [18]` and `nop [16]`).
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] Regarding the missing `hsync`:
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] Your `hblank` section drives the pin low (`set pins, 0`, `set pindirs, 1`) for the entire 12 µs. A
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] standard PAL signal requires the blanking interval to be split:
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Front porch: ~1.5 µs at black level (float / `set pindirs, 0`)
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Horizontal sync: ~4.7 µs at sync level (drive low / `set pindirs, 1`)
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Back porch: ~5.8 µs at black level (float / `set pindirs, 0`)
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] If you hold the sync level for the full 12 µs, the monitor will not detect the pulse edge properly
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] and will fail to sync.
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] Finally, keep in mind that your setup instructions (`set`, `in`, `mov`, and the pre-`jmp`) add 10
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] cycles of overhead per line. To maintain exactly 9,600 cycles per line, you will need to subtract
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 10 cycles from your hblank/porch delays.
2026-03-29 09:37:19 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:40:35 [simon@midnightblue] i want to generate more stripes, thinner, and hit the 7800 dead on
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] Your math for the active line was spot on (39 cycles × 200 iterations = 7800 cycles), but there
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] were two small PIO quirks throwing off the timing:
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Off-by-one iteration: `set y, 25` and `in y, 29` puts exactly `200` into the ISR.
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] However, a `jmp y--, label` loop runs `Y + 1` times (so it ran 201 times). We can fix this by
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] adding a single `jmp y--, stripe` right before the loop to silently decrement `Y` to 199.
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Loop cycle count: The original `stripe` loop took 42 cycles instead of 39. Adjusting the
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] `nop` values brings it to exactly 39 cycles.
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] To fit within the 32-instruction limit of the PIO while perfectly balancing the horizontal timing
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] (~9600 cycles per line), I've removed the initial pin setups (they naturally wrap around from the
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] end of `hblank` with the correct sync level) and slightly optimized the blanking loops.
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the corrected PIO code:
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; pico2 pio = 150mhz
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] .program vidblit
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap_target
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; The initial sync state wraps around from hblank naturally
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	isr, null
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	y, 24
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] vblank:
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	x, 24
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	in	x, 28
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	x, isr		; X = 384 (385 iterations)
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] vseg:
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop	[23]		; 24 + 1 = 25 cycles
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x--, vseg	; 385 * 25 = 9625 cycles
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, vblank
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; display = 288 x 9600 = (9<<5) x 9600 cycles
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	x, 9
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	in	x, 27
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	x, isr
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] active:
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; active = 52 µs = 7,800 cycles = 200 stripes x 39 cycles
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 1
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pindirs, 0
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	y, 25
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	in	y, 29
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	y, isr		; Y = 200
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, stripe	; Decrement Y to 199 for exactly 200 iterations
2026-03-29 09:44:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
