2026-03-29 14:05:59 [simon@midnightblue] reset_usb_boot(0, 0) does not stop the pio
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] `resetusbboot` is declared in `<pico/bootrom.h>`.
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] If you are seeing `ReadBootSel` in examples online, it is usually a custom function because the
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] BOOTSEL button is not a standard GPIO (it shares the Flash Chip Select pin).
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] To ensure the PIO stops driving the video pin when resetting, you must explicitly disable the state
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] machine and release the GPIO back to a high-impedance input before calling the bootrom reset.
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here are reusable functions to handle reading the button and safely resetting:
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include <pico/bootrom.h>
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include <hardware/sync.h>
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include <hardware/structs/ioqspi.h>
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include <hardware/structs/sio.h>
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] // Safely reads the BOOTSEL button state via the QSPI chip select pin
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] bool readBootselButton() {
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	const uint CS_PIN_INDEX = 1;
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	uint32_t flags = save_and_disable_interrupts();
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	hw_write_masked(&ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].ctrl,
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					GPIO_OVERRIDE_LOW << IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_LSB,
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_BITS);
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Delay to allow pin state to settle
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for (volatile int i = 0; i < 1000; ++i);
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	bool buttonState = !(sio_hw->gpio_hi_in & (1u << CS_PIN_INDEX));
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	hw_write_masked(&ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].ctrl,
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					GPIO_OVERRIDE_NORMAL << IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_LSB,
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_BITS);
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	restore_interrupts(flags);
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	return buttonState;
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] // Disables PIO and floats the video pin before handing over to the bootrom
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] void rebootToUsb(PIO pio, int sm, uint pin) {
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, false);
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	gpio_set_function(pin, GPIO_FUNC_NULL);
2026-03-29 14:06:25 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	gpio_set_dir(pin, GPIO_IN);
