2026-03-30 09:01:03 [simon@midnightblue] today am learning about dma with c++ sdk
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] Great! DMA (Direct Memory Access) is a powerful feature on the RP2350 that allows data transfers
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] without CPU involvement. Let me give you a quick overview:
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] • Key DMA concepts on RP2350:*
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] - 12 independent DMA channels
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] - Memory-to-memory, memory-to-peripheral, peripheral-to-memory transfers
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] - Configurable triggers (timers, GPIO, peripherals)
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] - Chainable transfers
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] • Basic DMA setup steps:*
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 1. Configure DMA channel
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 2. Set source and destination addresses
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 3. Configure transfer count and control
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 4. Set triggers
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 5. Start transfer
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] Would you like:
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 1. A simple DMA memory copy example?
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 2. DMA with ADC or PWM?
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 3. Understanding DMA chaining?
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 4. Something specific you're working on?
2026-03-30 09:01:09 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:04 [simon@midnightblue] can i keep a fifo to pio fed repeating large block?
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] Yes! You can use DMA to continuously feed a PIO FIFO with a repeating data block. This is a common
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] pattern for streaming data to PIO.
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] • Key approach:*
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] - Use DMA's chaining or ring buffer mode
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] - Configure DMA to reload the same source buffer
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] - Trigger on PIO FIFO availability
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:19 [deepseek-chat] • Example structure:*
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] #include "hardware/dma.h"
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] #include "hardware/pio.h"
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] // 1. Set up PIO program with TX FIFO
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] // 2. Create data buffer
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] uint32_t data_buffer[BUFFER_SIZE];
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] // 3. Configure DMA channel
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] int dma_chan = dma_claim_unused_channel(true);
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] dma_channel_config c = dma_channel_get_default_config(dma_chan);
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] // Memory to peripheral (PIO TX FIFO)
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] channel_config_set_transfer_data_size(&c, DMA_SIZE_32); // Match PIO FIFO width
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] channel_config_set_read_increment(&c, true); // Increment source
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] channel_config_set_write_increment(&c, false); // Fixed destination (PIO FIFO)
2026-03-30 09:02:20 [deepseek-chat] channel_config_set_ring(&c, true, BUFFER_SIZE_BITS); // Ring buffer mode
