2026-03-30 09:03:58 [simon@midnightblue] must be power of 2?
2026-03-30 09:05:53 [simon@midnightblue] the buffer i am sending is 2+39*312 words longs
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] No, ring buffer mode requires power-of-2 sizes, but you don't need to use ring mode for
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] your case.
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] For your buffer (2 + 39*312 = 12170 words), you have better options:
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] • Option 1: DMA Chaining* (Recommended)
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - Configure DMA to transfer your exact buffer size
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - Set up a second "reload" control block that points back to start
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - DMA will chain back and repeat indefinitely
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] • Option 2: Double Buffering*
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - Use two DMA channels
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - Ping-pong between buffers
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - CPU can update one while DMA sends the other
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] • Option 3: Manual Reload*
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - Use DMA completion interrupt
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] - In ISR, restart DMA with same buffer
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] • Chaining example structure:*
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] dma_channel_config c = dma_channel_get_default_config(dma_chan);
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] // ... basic config ...
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] // Create control block for reload
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] dma_channel_config c_reload = c; // Copy config
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] // Point back to start of buffer
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] // Configure as chain-to address
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] // Set chain-to on main channel
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] channel_config_set_chain_to(&c, dma_chan_reload);
2026-03-30 09:06:01 [deepseek-chat] 
