2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] I see you're generating PAL video with PIO! Nice work. The CPU is currently feeding the PIO FIFO in
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] a busy loop. DMA would free up the CPU completely.
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] • Key observations:*
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] - Your buffer is 12170 words (2 + 39*312)
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] - PIO expects continuous streaming
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] - Current approach: `while (!piosmistxfifo_full())` loop
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] • DMA Implementation:*
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] #include "hardware/dma.h"
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] int dma_chan;
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] dma_channel_config dma_cfg;
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] void setup_dma() {
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_chan = dma_claim_unused_channel(true);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_cfg = dma_channel_get_default_config(dma_chan);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Memory to PIO TX FIFO
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	channel_config_set_transfer_data_size(&dma_cfg, DMA_SIZE_32);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	channel_config_set_read_increment(&dma_cfg, true);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	channel_config_set_write_increment(&dma_cfg, false);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Trigger when PIO TX FIFO has space
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	channel_config_set_dreq(&dma_cfg, pio_get_dreq(pio, VidStateMachine, true));
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Configure DMA but don't start yet
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_channel_configure(
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 		dma_chan,
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 		&dma_cfg,
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 		&pio->txf[VidStateMachine], // PIO TX FIFO
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 		frame,                       // Source buffer
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 		wordCount,                   // Transfer count (12170)
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 		false                        // Don't start immediately
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] // In main(), replace the while loop:
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] setup_dma();
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] while (!ReadBootSel()) {
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Start DMA transfer
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_channel_set_write_addr(dma_chan, &pio->txf[VidStateMachine]);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_channel_set_read_addr(dma_chan, frame);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_channel_set_trans_count(dma_chan, wordCount, true);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Wait for DMA to complete
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	dma_channel_wait_for_finish_blocking(dma_chan);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Update frame[1] for next frame
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	frame[1] = 1 + ((f++ & 1) * 4800);
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	// Toggle LED
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 	gpio_put(LED_PIN, !gpio_get(LED_PIN));
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] • Benefits:*
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] - CPU free during transfer (can do other work)
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] - Consistent timing
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] - Lower power consumption
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] • Note: You might want to use double buffering* if updating frame while DMA is
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] transferring. Want me to show that approach?
2026-03-30 09:08:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:45 [simon@midnightblue] no code just discussion please
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] Understood. Let's discuss the DMA approach for your video generator:
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • Current CPU-bound approach:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - You're manually pushing 12170 words per frame
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - CPU stuck in `while (!piosmistxfifo_full())` loop
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - ~50ms per frame at 150MHz (PAL is 20ms/frame)
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • DMA advantages:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 1. Free CPU - Can update next frame while DMA streams current
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 2. Deterministic timing - No CPU jitter affecting video signal
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 3. Power efficient - CPU can sleep during transfer
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • Key considerations:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • Buffer management:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] Your 12170-word buffer isn't power-of-2, so ring mode won't work. Options:
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 1. Single buffer with restart - DMA completes, CPU updates, restart DMA
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 2. Double buffering - While DMA sends buffer A, CPU updates buffer B
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 3. Chaining - Complex but allows continuous streaming
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • Timing constraints:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - PAL frame = 20ms
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - DMA transfer time for 12170 words ≈ ?
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - Need to ensure DMA keeps up with PIO consumption
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • Potential issues:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - DMA might starve PIO if not fast enough
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - CPU updates might interfere with DMA if same buffer
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] - Need proper synchronization
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] • Recommendation:*
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] Start with single buffer + DMA wait. Simple and works with your exact buffer size. Later
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] add double buffering if you need CPU time for graphics updates.
2026-03-30 09:09:54 [deepseek-chat] 
