2026-03-30 09:10:34 [simon@midnightblue] for interlace i may want to layout memory as bitmap and dma odd lines then evenlines
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] Exactly! For interlaced video, you'd want to separate odd and even fields in memory. The RP2350 DMA
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] can handle this elegantly.
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] • Memory layout options:*
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] • Option A: Separate buffers*
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] odd_field[wordCount/2]  // Lines 1, 3, 5...
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] even_field[wordCount/2] // Lines 2, 4, 6...
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Simple addressing
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Easy to update fields independently
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Two DMA configurations needed
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] • Option B: Interleaved in single buffer*
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] frame[wordCount] = {odd_line0, even_line0, odd_line1, even_line1...}
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Single buffer
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - DMA with stride/skip for field extraction
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - More complex addressing
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] • DMA approach for Option A:*
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 1. Two DMA channels - One for odd, one for even fields
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 2. Alternate triggers - Based on field sync in PIO
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 3. Chain or restart - After each field completes
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] • PIO considerations:*
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Your PIO program would need field identification
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Different sync patterns for odd/even fields
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - DMA trigger on field change
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] • Timing:*
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Each field = 10ms (half of 20ms frame)
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - DMA must transfer 6085 words per field
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] - Field blanking period for buffer switch
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] This is a classic video processing pattern. The RP2350's DMA is well-suited for it with proper
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] configuration.
2026-03-30 09:10:43 [deepseek-chat] 
