2026-03-30 09:12:34 [simon@midnightblue] please explain support for stride skip in dma
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] The RP2350 DMA supports stride/skip through the `READADDR` and `WRITEADDR` reload
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] registers. This allows you to skip over memory when transferring non-contiguous data.
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • How it works:*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 1. Primary transfer: Moves data from source to destination
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 2. Address reload: After each transfer, addresses jump by a stride value
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 3. Use case: Perfect for de-interlacing or accessing every Nth element
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • Key registers:*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - `READADDR` / `WRITEADDR`: Current transfer address
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - `READADDRRELOAD` / `WRITEADDRRELOAD`: Value to reload after transfer completes
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - Transfer count controls how many elements per "row"
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • Example: Skip every other line (interlaced extraction)*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] Memory: [Line0, Line1, Line2, Line3, Line4...]
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] Stride: 2 * line_size_words
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] Result: [Line0, Line2, Line4...] (odd field)
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • Limitations on RP2350:*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - Stride is set via reload registers, not a dedicated stride register
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - You need to calculate: `reloadaddr = currentaddr + stride`
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - Works best with chaining for complex patterns
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • For your 39 words per line:*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - To extract odd lines: Stride = 78 words (2 lines)
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] - To extract even lines: Start at line 1, same stride
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • Alternative approach:*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] Use two DMA channels with different starting addresses. Often simpler than stride
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] calculations.
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] • Practical advice:*
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] For video interlacing, separate buffers (Option A) is usually cleaner than stride tricks. The DMA
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] can easily switch between two buffers without complex addressing math.
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] Would you like the register-level details for implementing stride, or are you leaning toward the
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] two-buffer approach?
2026-03-30 09:12:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:20 [simon@midnightblue] does pico support separating memory into banks for optimal usage patterns
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] The RP2350 has a single unified SRAM (264KB), not separate banks like some
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] microcontrollers. However, there are optimization patterns:
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • Memory organization:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - 264KB SRAM - Contiguous address space
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - 8KB ROM - Bootrom with utility functions
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - DMA can access all SRAM equally
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • Optimization strategies:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • 1. Cache-friendly layout:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Place frequently accessed data together
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - DMA buffers aligned to cache lines (32 bytes)
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • 2. DMA-efficient patterns:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Align buffers to 32-bit boundaries (DMA requirement)
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Place buffers in different cache ways to reduce contention
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • 3. SRAM partitioning (manual):*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] // Example manual partitioning
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] #define VIDEO_BUF_START  0x20000000
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] #define AUDIO_BUF_START  0x20010000
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] #define DATA_BUF_START   0x20020000
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • 4. Cache considerations:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - RP2350 has 16KB cache (2-way set associative)
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - DMA bypasses cache (unless using XIP flash)
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Consider cache aliasing if buffers share cache sets
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • 5. DMA priority:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - 12 channels with configurable priority
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Can group channels for video/audio/data
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • For your video application:*
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Place frame buffer in SRAM
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Ensure 32-bit alignment for DMA
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] - Consider placing other buffers in different cache "ways" if performance critical
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] • No hardware banks*, but you can manually organize memory for optimal DMA/cache
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] performance. The unified SRAM simplifies programming but requires thoughtful layout for
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] high-bandwidth applications like video.
2026-03-30 09:14:31 [deepseek-chat] 
