2026-03-30 09:15:57 [simon@midnightblue] is there a nature pal pixel clock frequency most digital tv will sample signal at?
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] Yes, there's a standard digital sampling frequency for PAL that modern digital TVs expect.
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] • PAL Digital Sampling (ITU-R BT.601):*
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Luminance (Y) sampling: 13.5 MHz (common for both PAL and NTSC)
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Color difference (Cb/Cr): 6.75 MHz (4:2:2) or 3.375 MHz (4:2:0)
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] • Why 13.5 MHz?*
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Derived from common multiple of PAL and NTSC line rates
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - PAL: 625 lines × 15625 Hz = 13.5 MHz ÷ 864
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - NTSC: 525 lines × 15734 Hz = 13.5 MHz ÷ 858
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Allows single digital standard for both systems
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] • Your PIO clock at 150 MHz:*
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - 150 MHz ÷ 13.5 MHz ≈ 11.111
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Not an integer ratio
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Common approach: Use 12 MHz (150 ÷ 12.5 = 12)
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - Or 12.5 MHz (150 ÷ 12 = 12.5)
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] • Practical considerations:*
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 1. TVs are tolerant - ±1000 ppm typical
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 2. Your current 9600 cycles/line:
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat]    - 150 MHz ÷ 9600 = 15.625 kHz (PAL line rate)
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat]    - Pixel clock: 150 MHz ÷ (9600/width) ≈ ?
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 3. For 1248 pixels active: 9600/1248 ≈ 7.69 cycles/pixel
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] • Recommendation:*
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] Aim for 12-13 MHz pixel clock. Adjust your PIO timing to get close to 13.5 MHz if possible,
2026-03-30 09:16:08 [deepseek-chat] but 12 MHz will work with most TVs.
