2026-03-30 09:36:46 [simon@midnightblue] 2 cycles for loop? are you sure
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] You're right to question that! Let me check the actual PIO timing:
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • PIO Instruction Timing:*
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - `out`: 1 cycle (execution) + delay
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - `jmp`: 3 cycles (1 execute + 2 delay when taken)
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • So:*
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] stripe:
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 	out pindirs, 1 [9]    ; 1 + 9 = 10 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 	jmp y--, stripe       ; 1 + 2 = 3 cycles (when taken)
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • Total:* 13 cycles per pixel iteration
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • For 704 pixels:*
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - 704 × 13 = 9,152 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - PAL active: 7,800 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - Overshoot: 1,352 cycles (9 µs!)
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • Even worse!* You need much shorter delays.
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • To fit 704 pixels in 7,800 cycles:*
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - Max cycles/pixel: 7,800 ÷ 704 ≈ 11.08 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - Need: `out` + `jmp` ≤ 11 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - `jmp` is 3 cycles, so `out` delay ≤ 8 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - Try `[7]`: 1+7=8 + 3 = 11 cycles ✓
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • With `[7]` delay:*
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - 704 × 11 = 7,744 cycles
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - Fits in 7,800 with 56 cycles margin
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] - Pixel clock: 150 ÷ 11 ≈ 13.64 MHz (good!)
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-30 09:36:55 [deepseek-chat] • Set `frame[0] = 704`* and use `[7]` delay. This should give clean vertical stripes.
