2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] You are very welcome! Here are the answers to your questions regarding the updated code:
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 1. Will the FIFO be not empty with the 10 bits in it?*
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] Yes. In your `ps2.pio` script, after shifting in the 8 data bits, 1 parity bit, and 1 stop bit, you
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] pad the Input Shift Register (ISR) with 22 zeros (`in null, 22`) and execute `push noblock`. This
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] explicitly pushes the completed 32-bit word into the RX FIFO. The moment that happens, the FIFO is
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] no longer empty, and your C++ check `!piosmisrxfifo_empty()` will correctly
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] trigger.
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 2. Is the default GPIO an input with Schmitt trigger?*
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] Yes. On the RP2040/RP2350, calling `gpio_init()` resets the pin to a high-impedance input.
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] Additionally, the hardware pads on the Pico have Schmitt triggers enabled by default upon reset,
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] which is perfect for reading the potentially noisy open-collector clock and data lines of a PS/2
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] device.
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 3. Will a mouse send through bytes similar to a keyboard?*
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] Yes, exactly the same. At the physical wire level, PS/2 mice and keyboards use the identical 11-bit
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] frame protocol (1 start bit, 8 data bits, 1 odd parity bit, 1 stop bit). Your PIO state machine
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] will read bytes from a mouse without any modifications. The only difference is how your C++ code
2026-03-30 20:12:03 [gemini-3.1-pro] interprets the data (key scancodes vs. 3-byte/4-byte mouse movement packets).
