2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] The Google API implementation is on the right track, mapping OpenAI-style payloads to Gemini's
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] structure. However, there are two key issues in `prepareGeminiPrompt` and one potential crash in
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] `connectGoogle` related to your recent tool calling and continuity fixes.
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Continuity Issue in `prepareGeminiPrompt`
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] In your `assistant` case, you are checking for `item.toolcallid` instead of
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] `item.toolcalls`. When the assistant makes a tool call, OpenAI format uses `toolcalls`.
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because of this typo, the code falls through to the `else` block and pushes an empty text part
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] instead of the required `functionCall` object, breaking Gemini's conversation history.
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] Additionally, in the `tool` case, Gemini expects the role to be `"function"`, not `"tool"`.
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the corrected switch block for `prepareGeminiPrompt`:
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			case "assistant": {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				if (item.tool_calls) {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					const parts = item.tool_calls.map(tc => ({
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						functionCall: {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 							name: tc.function.name,
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 							args: JSON.parse(tc.function.arguments)
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						}
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					}));
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					contents.push({ role: "model", parts });
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				} else {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					contents.push({ role: "model", parts: [{ text: item.content || "" }] });
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				}
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				break;
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			}
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			case "tool": {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				const functionResponse = { name: item.name, response: JSON.parse(text) };
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				if (debugging) echo("[GEMINI] functionResponse", functionResponse);
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				contents.push({ role: "function", parts: [{ functionResponse }] });
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				break;
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			}
