2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Potential Crash in `connectGoogle`
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] When Gemini decides to call a function, it often omits text entirely. Calling `await
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] result.response.text()` will throw an error if no text parts exist in the response, terminating the
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] relay.
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] You should wrap the text extraction in a try-catch block:
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						let text = "";
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						try {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 							text = await result.response.text();
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						} catch (e) {
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 							// Ignored: model returned a pure tool call without text
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						}
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						const usage = result.response.usageMetadata || {};
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						const choices = [];
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						choices.push({ message: { content: text || null } });
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						const calls = result.response.functionCalls();
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] With these adjustments, the model's tool calls will be properly formatted as `functionCall` objects
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] in the history, the tool results will be returned as `functionResponse` parts, and the strict
2026-03-30 21:33:14 [gemini-3.1-pro] alternating continuity required by the Gemini API will be maintained.
