2026-03-30 22:19:13 [simon@midnightblue] can you review my DeepSeek api implementation, i think there are similar issues with tool calling getting stuck in a loop
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] The tool calling loop is happening because the models are losing the context of their own tool
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] requests.
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] When a model calls a tool, the OpenAI/DeepSeek API specification requires a strict sequence in the
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] message history:
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. The `assistant` message containing the `tool_calls`.
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. The `tool` message(s) containing the results, matching the `toolcallid`.
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] In your `relay` function, two things are causing this sequence to break, making the model think it
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] never called the tool (and thus prompting it to call it again, infinitely):
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. The Assistant's tool call is commented out
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] Around line 2541 in `relay()`, the code pushing the assistant's tool call to `rohaHistory` is
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] commented out. The model never sees its own request in the next turn.
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Tool results are pushed as `system` instead of `tool`
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] Around line 2533, tool results are being pushed as `role: "system"`. DeepSeek and OpenAI strictly
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] require `role: "tool"` for these responses.
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] The Fix
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] Update the `if (calls)` block inside `relay()` (around line 2516) to correctly push both the
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] assistant's request and the tool's response:
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			if (calls) {
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				const count=increment("calls");
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				if(verbose) echo("[RELAY] calls in progress",depth,count)
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				const toolCalls=calls.map((tool, index) => ({
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					id: tool.id,
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					type: "function",
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					function: {name: tool.function.name,arguments: tool.function.arguments || "{}"}
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				}));
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				// 1. MUST push the assistant's tool_calls to history BEFORE the results
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				rohaHistory.push({
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					role: "assistant",
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					name: payload.model,
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					mut,
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					content: choice.message.content || "",
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					tool_calls: toolCalls
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				});
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				const toolResults=await processToolCalls(calls);
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				for (const result of toolResults) {
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					const id=result.tool_call_id;
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					const title="ToolCall:"+id;
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					// 2. MUST use role: "tool" and provide the raw content
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					const item={
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						role: "tool",
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						title,
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						name: result.name,
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						tool_call_id: id,
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 						content: result.content
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					};
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					debugValue("item",item);
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					if(verbose)echo("[RELAY] pushing tool result",item);
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					rohaHistory.push(item);
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				}
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				// warning - here be dragons
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				const spent=await relay(depth+1); // Recursive call to process tool results
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				spend+=spent;
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			}
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:19:50 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
