2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] Thank you for sharing your code. I have reviewed `slopprompt.ts` and noted a few areas for
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] potential improvement:
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. UTF-8 Chunk Splitting: In `processUtf8`, if a multi-byte character sequence is split
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] across sequential `reader.read()` chunks, the `i + bytesNeeded <= value.length` check will fail. It
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] currently falls through to single-byte handling, which will corrupt the character. Buffering
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] incomplete sequences between reads would resolve this.
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Timer Accumulation: Inside the `slopPrompt` `while` loop, `timerPromise` creates a new
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] `setTimeout` on every iteration. Because unresolved timeouts are not cleared when another promise
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] wins the race, this will accumulate pending timers and bloat the event loop.
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Connection Cleanup: When a socket throws an error in `slopPrompt`'s race resolution,
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] `delete slopConnections[name]` is called, but the socket itself is not explicitly closed. This
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] could leave file descriptors open.
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] Your grapheme segmentation and terminal width calculations are very robust. Please let me know if
2026-03-30 22:27:51 [gemini-3.1-pro] you would like specific code adjustments for any of these points.
